Merry (fill in your favorite religous holiday)
Happy New Year (for all of those using the same calendar I do)
Good Day (for anyone not covered by one of the above two)

A couple of orders of business.

1) Obviously, here's the new file list that covers Dec 11 - Jan 1. With
exams, holidays, and R&R, it took a while to get this out. Send corrections
to ewt@sunsite.unc.edu

2) I've heard a lot of negative comments about SLS. To respond to this, 
sunsite now mirrors the latest TAMU and Slackware distributions from their
home sites (note that we *don't* have all of the TAMU source code though).
Now all of the major linux distributions (SLS, MCC, TAMU, Slackware)
are in /pub/Linux/distributions on sunsite. 

3) More on SLS. It's been moved from SLS/ to SLS.old/. I would really like
to remove that unless I hear some good reasons not to. Good reasons
would be a note from Peter MacDonald saying it might be upgraded eventually 
or a large outpouring of sentiment from people in general. So everyone
who wants to see SLS kept/killed, send me a note via email and let me know
your thoughts. Don't nother discussing this in the newsgroups though, as
I promise not to read any of it. 

Thoughts to ewt@sunsite.unc.edu.

