procps-0.9 has been released, and is now available from
tsx-11.mit.edu:/pub/linux/BETA/procps/procps-0.9.tar.gz, and will be
available in time from sunsite.unc.edu somewhere.

Procps is a collection of utilities which gather their information
from the /proc filesystem, including ps, w, free, uptime, top, tload,
fuser, killall, pstree, XConsole, xload, xmem, and xidle.

This version adds some new functionality, as well as fixing some
rather large bugs perpetrated in the latest version, especially a
w that didn't know what anyone was doing.  Furthermore, JCPU should
now work more correctly with w.

Please read the README before doing installing -- it really does
contain important information.  A copy is appended to this message.

